# Plan — etude-n9b.2 checkout isolation and seat prompt

Goal: consume the gated `read_checkout` contract so the shared seat prompt keeps
model seats output-only by default and explicitly authorizes reproducible reads
only after a workflow grant, while placing the measurement-authority rule in the
exact prompt every seat reads.

ANCESTOR: etude-n9b (P1) — deliver GitHub issue #16 as an opt-in checkout-read
verification capability without changing the default. MEASUREMENT: today both
`GateStage` and live `runGate` call `runGateSeats` with the checkout as every
seat's process working directory, while the shared prompt has no explicit
output-only-versus-read authorization or measurement rule.

BLAST RADIUS: none: worktree and repo only. Tests create and remove private temp
git repositories. No host package, system path, container, shared service,
credential, external state, new worktree, or large artifact is created.

## Build decision

Build. The contract child establishes a per-gate boolean; this child makes that
boolean part of the prompt authorization every trusted registry harness receives.
The existing live-run checkout cwd is already the read primitive, so no new
filesystem proxy or pseudo-sandbox is needed.

## Runtime design

1. Thread `gate.ReadCheckout` through both gate paths into one
   `buildGatePrompt` call used for every model seat.
2. For false or absent, the prompt says `CHECKOUT ACCESS: OUTPUT-ONLY`, directs
   the seat not to inspect the process checkout, and states that only the inlined
   artifact and embedded provenance are authorized evidence. Keep the existing
   cwd unchanged; cwd is not claimed as a sandbox.
3. For true in a live run, the prompt says `CHECKOUT ACCESS: READ-ONLY` and names
   the pinned commit already recorded by the run. Supervised `etude gate`
   reviews a possibly uncommitted caller tree and has no reproducible checkout
   containing that work, so `GateStage` fails closed with a clear "live run
   workflows only" error before seats or checks. It creates no second worktree.
   Ordinary supervised output-only gates remain unchanged, and their
   deterministic checks continue in the caller tree.
4. Until GitHub issue #14 lands, a live read grant enumerates the pinned tree's
   actual gitlink entries (mode 160000), not the `.gitmodules` proxy, and fails
   closed before any seat runs when one exists. This is justified by the
   measured #14 defect: a bug was filed against tests that appeared absent in an
   unpopulated submodule checkout but passed 40/0 at the same commit after
   population. Replace this temporary refusal with #14's populated-and-recorded
   proof after rebase.
5. Record the resolved boolean on every `GateAttempt` created by either gate
   path. False stays omitted from JSON by the schema contract; true is durable.
6. Build one identical prompt for all seats through one shared builder. It
   states the resolved access mode
   and carries this rule verbatim in substance:
   - embedded provenance is AUTHORITATIVE for measurements;
   - seats must not re-derive arithmetic because provenance is embedded so they
     do not;
   - checkout reads exist to falsify a stage-output claim, not recompute it;
   - when checkout evidence shows the output wrong, return BLOCK with evidence
     instead of silently substituting new numbers.

The prompt carries the rule even on output-only gates. Registry seat commands
are the trusted enforcement boundary for prompt/tool policy; model conclusions
remain untrusted review votes. Arbitrary deliberate host-path scanning by a
misconfigured command is outside this feature's boundary and is not falsely
claimed to be prevented by cwd selection.

## Complete call-site set

- `Engine.GateStage` in `internal/liverun/gate_once.go` (supervised gate).
- `Engine.runGate` in `internal/liverun/gate.go` (live run and forward replay).
- `runGateSeats` is the single execution helper both paths share.
- `buildGatePrompt` becomes the single prompt builder used by both paths.
  Live-run checks keep the stage-output input they already consume, while model
  seats receive the shared prompt. The implementation gate must verify no model
  seat path emits an input without the rule.

